\begin_layout Section
Harnessing the VS Code SVD View
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To verify that the compiler isn't dropping write operations or operating on temporary local copies:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
1.
 Look at the VS Code Debug pane on the left-hand sidebar during an active breakpoint.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
2.
 If a standard cortex-debug extension is installed look for the Cortex Peripherals or X域 (SVD) Variables view.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
3.
 Expand SIO → GPIO_OE and GPIO_OUT.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
4.
 Step over Initialize_gSPI.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

If those fields do not visually light up with the target masks it confirms that the SVD variable initialization statement is modifying local stack memory instead of absolute register memory.
 [1,
 2] 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Ensuring Volatile Assignment
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If you step code in the VS Code debugger and watch fields inside RP.SIO.Periph fail to update,
 it means you need to avoid "Read-Modify-Write" record structures that confuse the compiler's optimizer.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Instead of passing record structures by value,
 modify fields by forcing direct absolute whole-word writes to the .all memory location,
 or use the atomic register fields exposed by the SVD.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For example,
 update your Write_gSPI_Byte loop inside your body file to write directly to the SVD's raw addresses:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
procedure Write_gSPI_Byte (Data :
 Unsigned_8) is
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Temp :
 Unsigned_8 := Data;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
begin
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
for Bit in 1 ..
 8 loop
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
-- Clear SCLK line
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
RP.SIO.Periph.GPIO_OUT_CLR.all := Mask_CLK;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
-- Set or Clear DATA line
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
if (Temp and 16#80#) /= 0 then
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
RP.SIO.Periph.GPIO_OUT_SET.all := Mask_DATA;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
else
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
RP.SIO.Periph.GPIO_OUT_CLR.all := Mask_DATA;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
end if;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
-- Use your working hardware timer counter for stable timing tracking
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Delay_Microseconds (2);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
-- Raise SCLK line
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
RP.SIO.Periph.GPIO_OUT_SET.all := Mask_CLK;
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Temp := Shift_Left (Temp,
 1);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Delay_Microseconds (2);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
end loop;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
end Write_gSPI_Byte;
\end_layout

